# Three stacked panels from quse.csv, sharing the time axis.
# Utilization, saturation, and error rate.
# Several queues: one hue per queue. Window 10 is light, 100 is solid,
# 1000 is dark and dashed.
# One queue: the slide colors. Blue utilization, a yellow saturation area,
# a red error rate.
# The legend sits beside the figure once. It names the three windows, and
# each queue when there is more than one.
# Saturation's 10-step series is a filled area. The 100 and 1000 series are lines.

function plot_use(quse, out):
    df = read quse.csv
    if qid filter is set: keep those queues
    fig = three panels sharing the time axis

    for qid, hue in zip(queues, palette):
        panel utilization: plot Utilization(10/100/1000), y from 0 to 1
        panel saturation: fill Saturation(10), plot Saturation(100/1000)
        panel error rate: plot Errors(10/100/1000)

    legend once, beside the panels
    save fig to out
